msgid ""
"Secure a Quarkus application with Basic authentication and Jakarta "
"Persistence"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Secure your Quarkus application endpoints by combining the built-in Quarkus "
"xref:security-basic-authentication.adoc[Basic authentication] with the "
"Jakarta Persistence identity provider to enable role-based access control "
"(RBAC).\n"
"The Jakarta Persistence `IdentityProvider` creates a `SecurityIdentity` "
"instance, which is used during user authentication to verify and authorize "
"access requests making your Quarkus application secure."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information about Jakarta Persistence, see the xref:security-jpa."
"adoc[Quarkus Security with Jakarta Persistence] guide."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This tutorial prepares you for implementing more advanced security "
"mechanisms in Quarkus, for example, how to use the OpenID Connect (OIDC) "
"authentication mechanism."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

msgid "To complete this guide, you need:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Roughly 15 minutes"
msgstr ""

msgid "An IDE"
msgstr ""

msgid "JDK 11+ installed with `JAVA_HOME` configured appropriately"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache Maven {maven-version}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally the xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] if you want to use it"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally Mandrel or GraalVM installed and xref:building-native-image."
"adoc#configuring-graalvm[configured appropriately] if you want to build a "
"native executable (or Docker if you use a native container build)"
msgstr ""

msgid "What you will build"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To demonstrate different authorization policies, the steps in this tutorial "
"guide you through building an application that provides the following "
"endpoints:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Endpoint"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "`/api/public`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The `/api/public` endpoint can be accessed anonymously."
msgstr ""

msgid "`/api/admin`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `/api/admin` endpoint is protected with role-based access control (RBAC)."
"\n"
"Only users granted with the `admin` role can access it.\n"
"At this endpoint, the `@RolesAllowed` annotation enforces the access "
"constraint declaratively."
msgstr ""

msgid "`/api/users/me`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `/api/users/me` endpoint is protected by RBAC.\n"
"Only users that have the `user` role can access the endpoint.\n"
"This endpoint returns the caller's username as a string."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To examine the completed example, download the {quickstarts-archive-"
"url}[archive] or clone the Git repository:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can find the solution in the `security-jpa-quickstart` link:{quickstarts-"
"tree-url}/security-jpa-quickstart[directory] in the upstream {ProductName} "
"community."
msgstr ""

msgid "Create and verify the Maven project"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For Quarkus Security to be able to map your security source to Jakarta "
"Persistence entities, ensure that the Maven project that is used in this "
"tutorial includes the `security-jpa` or the `security-jpa-reactive` "
"extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"xref:hibernate-orm-panache.adoc[Hibernate ORM with Panache] is used to store "
"your user identities but you can also use xref:hibernate-orm.adoc[Hibernate "
"ORM] with the `security-jpa` extension.\n"
"Both xref:hibernate-reactive.adoc[Hibernate Reactive] and xref:hibernate-"
"reactive-panache.adoc[Hibernate Reactive with Panache] can be used with the "
"`security-jpa-reactive` extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You must also add your preferred database connector library.\n"
"The instructions in this example tutorial use a PostgreSQL database for the "
"identity store."
msgstr ""

